    "01e56e4b2ffae22da581e9c98e54ba08806bcb478ab053f8450fc428314abd0d": {
      "normalizationVersion": 1,
      "sourceHash": "7be10947e065564a106a76f2be48c9e24709f144810c6a5fa8e544324a331fbd",
      "contextFingerprint": "f8b9a5afdc8f16cfb948c8e9941a2a22397fdda9e7d540c784075a0400d3df6f",
      "sourceText": "- **左值**：有名字、可以取地址的对象。如变量 `x`、`arr[0]`。\n- **右值**：临时的、即将销毁的对象。如 `42`、`x + y`、`std::move(x)`。\n- **右值引用 `T&&`**：绑定到右值的引用。\n- **移动语义**：通过\"偷\"右值的资源而不是拷贝，来避免不必要的深拷贝。\n- **`std::move`**：将左值转为右值引用，告诉编译器\"这个对象我以后不再用了，你可以偷它的资源\"。",
      "translatedText": "- **lvalue** : An object that has a name and whose address can be taken\\. For example, variables `x`、`arr[0]`。\n- **rvalue** : A temporary object that is about to be destroyed\\. For example, `42`、`x + y`、`std::move(x)`。\n- **rvalue reference `T&&`** : A reference bound to an rvalue\\.\n- **Move semantics** : Avoid unnecessary deep copies by \"stealing\" the resources of an rvalue instead of copying them\\.\n- **`std::move`** : Converts an lvalue to an rvalue reference, telling the compiler, \"I will not use this object again, so you can steal its resources\\.\"",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 225,
        "outputTokens": 128,
        "costUsd": 0.000222
      }
